# Spatial document placement (the human override layer)
#
# The base `*.diagram.json` / `*.scene.json` is committed; this layer is not.
# A diagram's layout is a deterministic function of its base document, so
# everyone opening one sees the same geometry without this file — what it holds
# is one person's deviation from that shared default, and drag coordinates have
# no meaningful merge resolution. Leaving it merely untracked is worse than
# either choice: AgentRoom's own dirty check runs
# `git status --untracked-files=all`, so an uncommitted placement file blocks a
# branch switch and the session-branch restore before a turn.
#
# Safe for the engine, which resolves this path from the base file and reads it
# directly rather than through the `git ls-files` index. The cost is that a
# curated arrangement cannot be shared at all: coordinates never enter the base
# document by design, so a diagram needing curation to be readable wants a
# narrower base diagram instead.
*.diagram.human.json
*.scene.human.json

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
